            <profile id="3a96-3a03-730a-59bc" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Bucellarii and Cavalry have a hand weapon and light armour. Eastern Shock Cavalry. They may have heavy armour (+1). In early armies, Bucellarii have kontos, composite bow and buckler (+7) and either half barding (+2) or barding (+4). In later armies, Bucellarii have thrusting spear, composite bow and shield (+8) and may have either half barding (+2) or barding (+4). Units other than Bucellarii may use Combined Formation with up to half their models exchanging thrusting spear for javelin (-2) or composite bow (-1) and forming the rear ranks. The Bucellarii must be led by the Army General at all times.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="b6fc-eb5b-0a57-d4eb" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
