  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="adac-2044-3947-8dc4" name="Early Byzantine (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #56 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The starting date for this list is the collapse of the western Roman Empire, at which point it is convenient to label the Eastern Empire’s armies as “Byzantine” rather than “Late Roman”. It covers the armies of Belisarius and Narses, that regained so much of the Western lands for Justinian, and those of Heraclius which fought off the Avars and Sassanids. It is divided into Early (E) and Late (L) variants. Allies: The following mercenary troops may be selected: Allies: The army may use Light Bolt Throwers (use the Late Roman entry without the cart) with the points taken from the AJlies allocation at the usual one model per 1,200 points. Allies: Allied contingents may also be taken from the Steppe Nomad list: Huns, Alans, Avars (E), Khazars (L).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Early Byzantine - Early Army]
  Allies: up to 33%
  Cavalry: at least 33%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: Up to 50% Cavalry: At least 33% Allies: Up to 33% May not take troops marked as (L). Any mounted figure may be fielded dismounted at –13 points. Dismounted cavalry are taken from the cavalry allocation. Formed Light Cavalry which dismount become Close Order Infantry and may form Shieldwall. Must take at least two bow-armed cavalry units.
[Early Byzantine - Early Byzantine]
  In armies exceeding 3,000 points the Magister may be upgraded to Emperor with Ld 10 (+100 points).
[Early Byzantine - Later Army]
  Allies: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 75%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Skirmishers: up to 10%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: Up to 50% Cavalry: Up to 75% Skirmishers: Up to 10% Allies: Up to 25% May not take troops marked as (E). Any mounted figure may be fielded dismounted at –13 points. Dismounted cavalry are taken from the cavalry allocation. Formed Light Cavalry which dismount become Close Order Infantry and may form Shieldwall.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
